s and also  how much they're going to eat or if they  eat it all now laying out a variety of  nutritious oatmeal toppings all of which  you as the parent feel good about  serving not only is super visually  appealing and also very fun but it also  increases the likelihood that something  will be consumed since the kids feel in  control they are the masters of their  breakfast are you taking over the house  yes you are not to mention serving food  family style is a great way to reduce  waste and also the power struggles that  often occur at the table so here we have  some leftover fruits and i'm just going  to add them into this freezer friendly  ziploc bag and put it in a freezer look  at that like no waste at all and i  actually do the same thing in my house  with like half eaten apples or bananas  or pears i just think like my kids  always want an apple or a banana and  they take like two bites of it before it  gets abandoned on a shelf somewhere so i  just chop it up and i freeze it for  smoothies the next day i just know that  i have this one last carrot in the  fridge that i wanted to use so i'm going  to use a wavy knife and cut them into  fry okay if you have a picky eater you  will be amazed the difference a new fun  shape can make my youngest o  uh has really always been a more  selective eater since he started solids  than my eldest e we've gone through many  veggie strikes around here and one of  the only things that gets us back on  track are little fun veggie cutters to  make different shapes so if you're  struggling with picky eating in your  house especially around things like  veggies my tip is to remove all the  pressure to eat them and instead  encourage vegetable play so for example  stack up the zucchini coins make a face  with the peas have a little sword fight  with a carrot stick we need to reduce  the anxiety before we can even have a  chance of our kids wanting to have a  taste and little fun food cutters or  silly utensils can be a great way to  play i ended up adding about a quarter  cup of pesto and now we're just going to  add our pasta and just stir it all up  together okay so this is another great  tip for introducing a new novel food we  call it fading so if you know that mac  and cheese is a sure-fire safe food that  your kids will almost always accept and  like adding in a teeny tiny bit of a new  sauce or a new spice or a little  vegetable and then increasing that  amount over time until maybe we have  like straight up pesto pasta is a great  way to expand a picky eaters palette and  then that was pretty much it my kids  really love this one yes the carrot  fries some slices of orange and a little  bit of ketchup this made quite a bit of  pesto mac and cheese my kids actually  took it to school and they had it for  after school lunch this meal looks  incredible so we've really got  everything that i would look for in a  balanced kids meal carbs in the pasta  protein the chicken fat in the pesto  cheese sauce plus some kind of fruit or  veggie and that brings me to another  really important feeding tip don't shy  away from dips even the really sugary  ones like ketchup dips are a great safe  bridge food to help encourage children  to try new foods on their plate even if  they just lick the dip off the food  they're learning to like the fact that  they put the food in their mouth is  often a huge win for families with picky  eaters so think about kids nutrition as  a long game i am personally way less  concerned with the amount of sugar in  the ketchup if in the end having ketchup  means they have a more varied and  therefore nutritious palette and diet  okay but let's bring it back to winnie  for a second and talk about her personal  way of eating so on this particular day  i'm estimating a completely normal  average amount of calories and fiber and  a healthy split of macros it was a short  video so we didn't get a whole lot of  commentary and maybe what night in day  videos should all be like that like show  me the food inspiration not the moral  baggage that seems to accompany every  eating decision you make  i would love to see more content that  just plainly says hey  this is what i like or this is what i  can afford or this is what i had in the  fridge or what was available to me and  just leave it at that and yeah winnie is  an amazing home chef and mom with  recipes that are inherently well  balanced and relatively simple and  accessible i also think she's got some  incredible kid meal ideas for families  who maybe feel like they're stuck making  the same four meals on rotation and  while she's not a pediatric dietitian  she actually utilizes a lot of the  feeding strategies that the experts in  this field recommend i also really  appreciate that despite kids meals kind  of being a large part of her brand i  don't really see her posting her kids a  lot online and you guys know i've talked  about my own reasons for keeping my  family out of my feeds but it almost  feels rare to see that nowadays in the  influencer world but i personally will  be coming back to winnie's platforms in  the future the next time that we are in  a meal rut like maybe tonight i don't  know what we're making for dinner so  winnie hit me up and on that note that  is all that i have for you guys today  and if you like this video be sure to  give it the thumbs up leave me a comment  below on who or what you'd like to see  me or few next subscribe to the channel  and i'll see you next time on abby's  kitchen bye  [Music]

